{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788222665,"nonce":"VsbbYEEceiAR2LLjReVgg01mAeE=","message":"The procedural hole this issue raised is now a HARD CRITERION on 4.3 — Evan,\n2026-08-31 (session 10).\n\n4.2 flagged that the emergency posture drafts and never undrafts. Evan has ruled\nthat M1 (`664e9b9`) must demonstrate the full draft → fight → undraft cycle and\nthat a completed undraft is pass/fail, not a report line. A drafted colonist does\nnot eat, sleep or work and no alert names it, so over ten days a forgotten\nundraft is a slow-motion wipe — and `SeekRegistry.ShouldSeek` requires\n`!pawn.Drafted`, so the colonist also silently drops out of the seek posture.\n\nPLAY-LOOP.md's raid-end path should make undraft an explicit step with a read-back\nrather than leaving it implied.\n\nAlso recorded here: `accept/4.2-play-loop.py`'s `final-undrafted` check already\nasserts exactly this shape — 0 drafted, 0 hostiles at run end — and its dig paths\nwere confirmed against `DigestVerb.ColonistSection`/`ThreatSection`. So the\nauditor is ready for the criterion; what it has never done is audit a REAL run,\nbecause no `RUNS/` directory exists. 4.3 is what produces one.","files":null}]}